  "ingredients": [
    "250 gram green cabbage (sliced thin)",
    "4 tablespoon butter",
    "1 teaspoon onion powder",
    "12 ounce pork tenderloin",
    "1 1/2 tablespoon curry powder",
    "1 cup canned coconut milk",
    "salt and pepper (to taste)"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "Gather and prep all ingredients. If shredding the cabbage, make sure to cut the cabbage thin enough. Peel silverskin off of pork tenderloin if it is on there.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/curried-cabbage-pork-tenderloin/#wprm-recipe-54717-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/Curried-Cabbage-and-Pork-Tenderloin-1.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add half of the butter and cabbage to a pan over medium heat. Season with salt and pepper to taste. Saute cabbage, stirring occasionally, until soft and slightly golden. Set aside and keep warm.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/curried-cabbage-pork-tenderloin/#wprm-recipe-54717-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/Curried-Cabbage-and-Pork-Tenderloin-2.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Slice the tenderloin into 1/2 to 3/4 inch thick pieces.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/curried-cabbage-pork-tenderloin/#wprm-recipe-54717-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/Curried-Cabbage-and-Pork-Tenderloin-3.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Season the pork slices with onion powder and salt and pepper to taste.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/curried-cabbage-pork-tenderloin/#wprm-recipe-54717-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/Curried-Cabbage-and-Pork-Tenderloin-4.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add the remaining half of the butter to a pan over medium heat. Once hot, add in the pork slices and brown on both sides, about 2 minutes on each side. Remove from pan and set aside, leaving any juices in the pan.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/curried-cabbage-pork-tenderloin/#wprm-recipe-54717-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/Curried-Cabbage-and-Pork-Tenderloin-5.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add the coconut milk and curry powder to the pan over medium-low heat and stir together well, until there are no lumps of spice remaining.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/curried-cabbage-pork-tenderloin/#wprm-recipe-54717-step-0-5",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/Curried-Cabbage-and-Pork-Tenderloin-6.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Once sauce has thickened slightly, add pork back over low heat and stir to coat. If pork is not cooked all the way through, cover and allow to finish.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/curried-cabbage-pork-tenderloin/#wprm-recipe-54717-step-0-6",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/Curried-Cabbage-and-Pork-Tenderloin-7.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve the pork and curry sauce with fried cabbage. Enjoy!",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/curried-cabbage-pork-tenderloin/#wprm-recipe-54717-step-0-7",
      "imageSource": null
    }
  ],
